1. Actuator allocation vs. distance-to-riser — the figure you're missing
Aggregate across all 15 trials: x-axis is distance to the riser (−0.8 m to +0.4 m), thrust on the left axis, wheel speed on the right, mean with a ±1σ band, vertical line at contact.

If the policy ramps thrust before contact and decays it after, that curve is the entire paper in one plot — and crucially it's continuous, with no step change anywhere. That's your mode-free claim made visual rather than asserted. A mode-switched controller would show a discontinuity at a threshold; yours won't.

Everything needed is already in your trial CSVs (pos_x/y, action_3, wheel_meas_*) plus the step position from make_step_map.py. It costs you nothing extra to collect.

