3. Energy–success Pareto front
One point per w_E ∈ {0, 0.25, 1, 2, 4}, success rate against energy per traverse, operating point marked. This is what justifies your title. If there's a knee, it's a great figure; if the front is flat, it's still a publishable finding and you report it honestly.

4. Actuator identification, 4 panels — your most distinctive asset

(a) thrust: bench points + degree-4 fit, RMSE 3.9e-3 N
(b) wheel:  commanded vs achieved, with the 23.6 rad/s ceiling and the
            saturated region shaded — this is the figure that explains
